WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.497
On this slide, we are focusing on inspect data types.

00:00:03.497 --> 00:00:08.267
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:14.532
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.532 --> 00:00:22.292
A data type tells Python what a value means and which operations are valid.

00:00:22.292 --> 00:00:28.002
Numeric values support arithmetic, strings represent text, and Boolean values represent True or False logic.

00:00:28.002 --> 00:00:31.187
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:31.187 --> 00:00:37.337
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:40.682
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:40.682 --> 00:00:45.693
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.
